{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Persistence is Key"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Do's & Dont's  "}, {"type": "position", "content": 10}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 10}, {"type": "level", "content": "B2.1"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Describe ways of solving problems and getting things done in social contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. "}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": " Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": " Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. "}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts."}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn9le10ob10re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words you use to talk about work and interviews."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Brainstorm bad things people do in interviews. Write a list of at least 3 - 5 things. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write a dialogue between two people. One person is describing bad things they have done in an interview and the other is talking about things they could've, should've or would've done. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "When you are finished, read the dialogue to a partner. "}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I write about bad interview manners."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I write a dialogue about the bad things that are done in interviews."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I use modals for past speculation."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I read my dialogue about an interview to a partner. "}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Speculating About The Past"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "When you want to talk about situations in the past in a hypothetical context (not real or necessarily true), you can use the structures <span class=\"italic\">would have</span>, <span class=\"italic\">should have </span> and <span class=\"italic\">could have</span>."}, {"type": "text", "content": "a. <span class=\"italic\">Could have</span> (+ past participle) means that something was possible in the past, or you had the ability to do something in the past, but that you didn't do it."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\"><span class=\"underline\">I could've used</span></span> your help before but you said you were busy.  (= I had the chance to ask for your help but I didn't) </span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "b. <span class=\"italic\">Should have</span> (+ past participle) means something would have been a good idea, but you didn't do it. You can use it to give advice about the past when you say it to someone else, or to express regret about what you did or didn't do when you're talking about yourself."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">You <span class=\"strong\"><span class=\"underline\">should've told</span></span> me you were having issues.  (= You didn't tell me but it was a good idea to tell me.)</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">You <span class=\"strong\"><span class=\"underline\">should've waited</span></span> downstairs or outside.  (=I regret not waiting downstairs or outside)</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "c. Use <span class=\"italic\">would have</span> ( + past participle) to talk about something you wanted to do but didn't. This is very similar to the third conditional, but we don't need an 'if clause'."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">You <span class=\"strong\"><span class=\"underline\">would've benefited</span></span> more had you contacted me earlier (= You didn't contact me; therefore, you didn't benefit from my advice). </span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "I<span class=\"underline\"> would've taken</span> some time to assist with interviews."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I<span class=\"underline\"> could've called</span> you."}, {"type": "example", "content": "You <span class=\"underline\">shouldn't have</span> said that."}, {"type": "example", "content": "You<span class=\"underline\"> could've mentioned</span> that you left for personal reasons. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "You <span class=\"underline\">could've kept</span> your mouth shut."}, {"type": "example", "content": "You <span class=\"underline\">should've waited</span> until you got the job offer. "}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Reported Speech"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use reported speech when you are saying (reporting)  what other people said. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "When you tell people what someone has said in the past, you generally make the verb tense 'more in the past'. You need to change the verb to the next past form. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example:<br/> <span class=\"strong\">Direct speech</span><br/>                            \t\t\t <ul><li><span class=\"italic\">My interview game is not up to snuff. </span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Reported speech</span><br/> <ul><li><span class=\"italic\">You told me your interview game was not up to snuff. </span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "When changing sentences from direct speech, check if you have to change the following:<br/> <ul><li>pronouns (I said \u2192 He said) <li>Present tense verbs  <li>Place and time expressions <li>Tenses (backshift \u2192 change to the past)"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Some reporting verbs and expressions commonly used are: <span class=\"strong\">say</span>, <span class=\"strong\">tell</span>, and <span class=\"strong\">ask</span>. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Other reporting verbs you can use are: <span class=\"strong\">comment</span>, <span class=\"strong\">suggest</span>, <span class=\"strong\">observe</span>, <span class=\"strong\">remark</span>, <span class=\"strong\">claim</span>. All these verbs follow the pattern: subject + verb (ed) + that + clause. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "You <span class=\"underline\">said</span> you were busy so I didn't bother asking."}, {"type": "example", "content": "One recruiter at the job fair <span class=\"underline\">commented</span> that it is rude."}, {"type": "example", "content": "A friend <span class=\"underline\">suggested</span> that I schedule my interviews in the morning. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "A friend who works in HR <span class=\"underline\">observed</span> that this is when you're likely to be successful and get the job."}, {"type": "example", "content": "A friend <span class=\"underline\">remarked</span> that I am always too early for the interview."}, {"type": "example", "content": "My father <span class=\"underline\">claimed</span> that turning up five to 10 minutes is the sweet spot for interviews."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to not be up to snuff"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to be not as good as it should be "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You told me your interview game is not up to snuff."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le10ob10aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to be rough around the edges"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "not very sophisticated or unpolished"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I'm a little rough around the edges and I could've used your help before but you were busy. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le10ob10aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "earnest"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "serious and determined"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You're earnest and eager."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le10ob10aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to not have the air"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a feeling or attitude that someone has "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:You don't have the air of someone who can do it alone."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le10ob10aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "with one hand tied behind your back"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to do something very easily"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I know you can do it with one hand tied behind your back."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le10ob10aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to put in a good word"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to tell someone about the good qualities a person has"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I know a few companies that are hiring so I'll put in a good word for you. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le10ob10aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "sweet spot"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the best possible place or combination of factors"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: My father claimed that turning up five to 10 minutes is the sweet spot for interviews."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le10ob10aud07"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "if you'll excuse me"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to do very well"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I aced my interview and got the job!"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le10ob10aud08"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "ace an interview"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to do very well"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I aced my interview and got the job!"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le10ob10aud09"}]}], "labs": [{"exercises": [{"template_override": 1, "stimuli_ids": [0], "type": "WLC", "questions": [], "img_path": "", "id": 0, "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"ty